{title: Take My Life and Let It Be}
{artist: Frances Ridley Havergal (1836-1879)}
{key: F}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[F]Take my life, and [C]let it be
[Bb]Consecrated, [C]Lord, to [F]Thee;
[F]Take my moments [Bb]and my days,
[Gm]Let them flow in [C]ceaseless [F]praise.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[F]Take my hands, and [C]let them move
[Bb]At the impulse [C]of Thy [F]love;
[F]Take my feet, and [Bb]let them be
[Gm]Swift and beauti[C]ful for [F]Thee.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[F]Take my voice, and [C]let me sing
[Bb]Always, only, [C]for my [F]King;
[F]Take my lips, and [Bb]let them be
[Gm]Filled with messages [C]from [F]Thee.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[F]Take my silver [C]and my gold,
[Bb]Not a mite would [C]I with[F]hold;
[F]Take my intellect, [Bb]and use
[Gm]Every power as [C]Thou shalt [F]choose.
{eov}
